# AIGW OS per-app experience: how connections are told apart (docs/app-experience.md).
# An ISP or OEM can change this file (apps.rules) without new code: agctl apps --reload.
#
# kind <Kind> <condition>...     the first rule that matches wins, top to bottom
#   over the connection's last looks (one every apps.poll s):
#   proto=udp,tcp,quic            quic is UDP to port 443; any when not given
#   port=3478-3481,5349           the far end's port
#   down=lo-hi  up=lo-hi          kbit/s, the mean each way
#   pps=lo-hi                     packets a second, both ways together
#   pkt=lo-hi                     the mean packet of the busier way, bytes
#   ratio=lo-hi                   up bytes per 100 down bytes
#   duty=lo-hi                    % of the looks with traffic
#   life=lo-hi                    seconds since the connection began
#   steady=N                      the packet rate's spread at most N%
#   looks=N                       how many of the last looks (3; at most 6)
#   named=1                       only when a family below named the server
#   iot=1                         only on a smart-home device (its type, or the iot zone)
#   conf=N                        how sure, in %, without a family's name (with one: +25)
# family <Name> <Kind>[,<Kind>] <server name suffix>...   (Name: _ for a space)
# browse <N>                      N new web connections a minute from a device is browsing
#
# Kinds: VoiceCall VideoCall ScreenShare VideoStreaming CloudGaming OnlineGaming LargeDownload
#        Browsing SmartHome

# real time, by the ports they use (calls.c's hints), then by their traits alone
kind ScreenShare proto=udp port=3478-3481,5349,8801-8810,19302-19309,16384-16402,9000 up=300-20000 ratio=250- conf=70
kind VideoCall proto=udp port=3478-3481,5349,8801-8810,19302-19309,16384-16402,9000 down=200-20000 pps=30- conf=75
kind VoiceCall proto=udp port=3478-3481,5349,8801-8810,19302-19309,16384-16402,9000 down=6-250 up=6-250 pps=8- conf=75
kind OnlineGaming proto=udp port=3074,3659,27000-27050,7000-7500,19132-19133 pps=10- down=2-3000 conf=75
kind CloudGaming proto=udp down=4000-120000 ratio=0-8 pps=300- conf=55
kind ScreenShare proto=udp up=400-20000 down=0-1500 ratio=300- pps=30- steady=80 conf=50
kind VideoCall proto=udp down=250-20000 up=40-20000 pps=60- ratio=5-1000 pkt=300- steady=70 conf=55
kind VoiceCall proto=udp down=8-300 up=8-300 pps=16-260 pkt=40-450 ratio=25-400 steady=60 conf=50
kind OnlineGaming proto=udp down=2-1500 up=2-800 pps=16-300 pkt=30-700 ratio=10-1000 steady=70 named=1 conf=50
# the rest: big and steady is a download, big and bursty a stream, a trickle on a smart-home device
kind LargeDownload proto=tcp,quic down=6000- ratio=0-6 pkt=1000- duty=100- steady=35 looks=4 conf=50
kind VideoStreaming proto=tcp,quic down=400-120000 ratio=0-8 pkt=700- looks=3 conf=50
kind SmartHome iot=1 down=0-64 up=0-64 life=60- conf=60
browse 4

# server-name families (from the name the device looked up, or the TLS/QUIC handshake)
family Zoom VideoCall,VoiceCall,ScreenShare zoom.us zoom.com zoomgov.com
family Teams VideoCall,VoiceCall,ScreenShare teams.microsoft.com teams.live.com skype.com lync.com
family Google_Meet VideoCall,VoiceCall,ScreenShare meet.google.com stun.l.google.com
family WhatsApp VoiceCall,VideoCall whatsapp.net whatsapp.com
family FaceTime VideoCall,VoiceCall facetime.apple.com
family Webex VideoCall,VoiceCall,ScreenShare webex.com
family Discord VoiceCall,VideoCall,ScreenShare discord.media discord.gg
family Signal VoiceCall,VideoCall signal.org
family YouTube VideoStreaming googlevideo.com youtube.com
family Netflix VideoStreaming nflxvideo.net netflix.com nflxso.net
family Prime_Video VideoStreaming aiv-cdn.net primevideo.com
family Disney+ VideoStreaming dssott.com disneyplus.com bamgrid.com
family Hotstar VideoStreaming hotstar.com hotstarext.com
family JioCinema VideoStreaming jiocinema.com
family Twitch VideoStreaming ttvnw.net twitch.tv
family GeForce_NOW CloudGaming nvidiagrid.net geforcenow.com
family Xbox_Cloud CloudGaming gssv-play-prod.xboxlive.com xcloud.xboxlive.com
family Xbox_Live OnlineGaming,LargeDownload xboxlive.com
family PlayStation OnlineGaming,LargeDownload playstation.net
family Steam OnlineGaming,LargeDownload steamserver.net valve.net steamcontent.com
family Riot_Games OnlineGaming riotgames.com
family Epic_Games OnlineGaming,LargeDownload epicgames.com epicgames.dev
family Roblox OnlineGaming roblox.com rbxcdn.com
family Battle.net OnlineGaming,LargeDownload battle.net blizzard.com
family Windows_Update LargeDownload windowsupdate.com delivery.mp.microsoft.com
family Apple_Updates LargeDownload swcdn.apple.com updates.cdn-apple.com
family Tuya SmartHome tuyaus.com tuyaeu.com tuyacn.com tuyain.com
family Ring SmartHome ring.com
family Philips_Hue SmartHome meethue.com
family Nest SmartHome nest.com
